#
#   Stroika's valgrind memcheck suppressions - empty on purpose.
#
#   Every earlier entry (135, in this file and the x86_64, armhf and BlockAllocation ones) was removed in 2026-09 (#1177,
#   #1167) after a full valgrind run on Ubuntu 26.04 matched none of them. Add an entry only for a report confirmed to be a
#   false positive or a third-party problem, with a comment saying where it was seen (platform, compiler, library version)
#   and why it is not a Stroika bug, so it can be dropped once that no longer applies. An entry that only one architecture
#   needs goes in Valgrind-MemCheck-Common-<ARCH>.supp, which Tests/Makefile picks up automatically when it exists.
#
